## 📱 Overview

The Car Fuel Management Application is a Java-based system designed to help customers purchase fuel through a managed repayment and discount system. The application tracks customer fuel purchases, validates customer and vehicle information, and rewards loyal customers with long-term fuel discounts.

The system combines vehicle registration validation, customer profiling, fuel quotation generation, repayment management, and customer reward benefits into one application.

This project was designed as an academic application that combines Java programming, object-oriented design, file handling, APIs, databases, multimedia, and business logic.

---

# 🎯 Purpose of the Application

The main purpose of the application is to:

- Allow users to purchase fuel at reduced rates
- Track customer fuel purchase history
- Reward loyal and consistent customers with discounts
- Validate South African users and vehicles
- Provide secure payment options
- Automate fuel quotation and repayment calculations

The application is focused on creating a smart fuel repayment system where customers gradually pay less over time if they consistently use the service.

---

# 👤 User Registration Process

Users must create an account before using the service.

## Registration Details Required

The system captures:

- Name and surname
- South African ID number
- Home address
- Car registration number

---

# ✅ Validations

## South African ID Validation

The ID number is validated against a custom-built Home Affairs system to ensure:

- The person is a valid South African citizen
- The user can be traced

---

## 🚗 Car Registration Validation

The vehicle registration number is validated with:

- Traffic Department
- SAPS (South African Police Service)

The system checks:

- If the vehicle is roadworthy
- If the vehicle has not been reported stolen

The application uses **Java File I/O** to read registration information from files.

---

## 📍 South African Province Registration Validation

The registration number must match South African province formats such as:

| Province | Example |
|----------|----------|
| Gauteng | CA 123-456 |
| KwaZulu-Natal | ND 123456 |
| Mpumalanga | MPM 123 MP |
| Western Cape | CY 123456 |

The system uses Java exception handling and validation logic to reject invalid registration formats.

---

# 📷 Vehicle Image Capture

The system captures a photo of the vehicle including its registration plate from either:

- Front view
- Back view

This image is stored for verification purposes.

---

# 🚘 Car Registration Process

After user registration, customers register their vehicles.

## Steps

### 1. Select Vehicle

The user selects a car model from a dropdown list.

The vehicle list and fuel tank capacities are obtained from the:

- Automobile Association of South Africa

---

### 2. Fuel Capacity Generation

The system automatically generates:

- Fuel tank capacity
- Estimated full tank fuel cost

---

### 3. Fuel Quotation

Fuel prices are retrieved from:

- PetroleumSA

The system calculates:

- Current fuel cost
- Repayment amount
- Discount eligibility

---

### 4. Accept or Decline Offer

The customer can:

- Accept the quotation
- Decline the quotation

If declined, the process ends.

---

### 5. Repayment Date Selection

The customer chooses a repayment date:

- Within 30 days
- Flexible date selection allowed

---

### 6. Payment Options

Customers can pay using:

- Debit order
- Bank card
- Google Pay
- Other electronic payment methods

---

# 💰 Fuel Benefits for Consistent Customers

The system rewards loyal customers.

## Rules

- Customers can purchase fuel once per month
- First-time users repay:
  - Full fuel amount + 25%
  - Total repayment = 125%

---

## 📉 Discount Progression

If customers pay successfully within 30 days:

- They qualify for a 6.25% discount
- The discount applies to future purchases
- Discounts continue improving over time

---

## 🎯 Long-Term Benefits

After consistent usage:

- Customers gradually pay less
- Discounts continue yearly
- Eventually customers may only pay:
  - 25% of the full fuel amount

The system keeps percentages consistent even when:

- Fuel prices increase
- Customers change vehicles

---

# ⚠️ Benefits for Non-Consistent Customers

Customers who use the service less frequently still receive benefits.

## Usage Between 4 and 11 Times Per Year

- Receive 2.5% discount in year 2
- Repayment becomes 122.5%

---

## Usage Less Than 3 Times Per Year

- Receive 1% discount in year 2
- Repayment becomes 124%

---

## Discount Adjustments

Discounts may:

- Stay the same
- Increase
- Reduce

Depending on customer consistency.

---

# 💳 Payment Integration

The application supports electronic payment systems such as:

- Debit Orders
- Google Pay
- Card Payments
- Other Payment APIs

The payment integration is part of the backend system.

